.SH "NAME"
nvme-check-tls-key \- Check a NVMe TLS PSK (deprecated)
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.sp
.nf
\fInvme\fR [<global\-options>] \fIcheck\-tls\-key\fR [\-\-keyring=<name> | \-k <name>]
                        [\-\-keytype=<type> | \-t <type>]
                        [\-\-hostnqn=<nqn> | \-n <nqn>]
                        [\-\-subsysnqn=<nqn> | \-c <nqn>]
                        [\-\-keydata=<key> | \-d <key>]
                        [\-\-identity=<id\-vers> | \-I <id\-vers>]
                        [\-\-compat | \-C]
.fi
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.sp
Deprecated alias for linknvme\-keys\-check\-tls[1], kept for scripts written against nvme\-cli versions older than 3\&.0\&.
.sp
One difference: the old \fIcheck\-tls\-key\fR also accepted \fI\-\-insert\fR/\fI\-i\fR to derive and store a \fIretained\fR key directly, but the new \fIcheck\-tls\fR never modifies the keyring \(em that functionality moved to linknvme\-keys\-insert\-tls[1]\&. Scripts relying on \fI\-\-insert\fR here will get an "unrecognized option" error and must switch to \fInvme keys insert\-tls\fR directly; all other options continue to work unchanged through this alias\&.
.sp
New scripts should use \fInvme keys check\-tls\fR instead\&. This alias prints a deprecation warning on stderr and may be removed in a future release\&.
.sp
See linknvme\-keys\-check\-tls[1] for the full option reference\&.
.SH "GLOBAL OPTIONS"
.sp
The following options are defined at the top\-level nvme command and are available to this subcommand:
.PP
\-\-dry\-run
.RS 4
Print the command that would be executed, but do not actually execute it\&.
.RE
.PP
\-\-no\-ioctl\-probing
.RS 4
Disable probing for 64\-bit IOCTL support\&.
.RE
.PP
\-\-no\-retries
.RS 4
Disable retry logic on transient errors\&.
.RE
.PP
\-o <fmt>, \-\-output\-format=<fmt>
.RS 4
Set the reporting format to
\fInormal\fR,
\fItabular, \*(Aqjson\fR, or
\fIbinary\fR\&. Only one output format may be used at a time\&.
.RE
.PP
\-\-output\-format\-version=<version>
.RS 4
Select the output format version\&. Version
\fI1\fR
uses the original field naming, while version
\fI2\fR
(default) provides more consistent and script\-friendly field names\&.
.RE
.PP
\-\-timeout=<ms>
.RS 4
Set the timeout for the command in milliseconds\&.
.RE
.PP
\-v, \-\-verbose
.RS 4
Increase the level of detail in the output\&. May be specified multiple times to further increase verbosity\&.
.RE
.sp
These options can also be set as machine\-wide defaults in nvme\-cli\&.conf(5)\&. A command\-line flag always overrides the file\&.
